Hmm. So better: when answered is non-empty, keep call verbatim AND continue scanning for its results beyond the cut? No — the results are in the kept tail already (untouched). The problem is only results within the droppable region that got separated. When does that happen? [call c1, user steer, result c1] with regionEnd = index of 'user steer'... regionEnd = NEWEST user message. If user steer is newest (index 1), regionEnd=1, loop processes only i=0 (call). Inner loop: j=1 < len && answered non-empty: messages[1] is UserMessage → break. answered={c1} → verbatim. i=j=1, loop ends (i==regionEnd). Tail = [user steer, result c1]. Result c1 survives in tail; repair hoists it to the verbatim call. 

