/// Whether [messageCount] reached the pre-emptive trigger for a
/// [learnedCap]: fires when the count is within [margin] of the cap, so a
/// host compaction pass runs BEFORE the provider refuses (AC4).
///
/// Pathological small caps stand down: a cap at or below the [margin] is
/// inside the fixed request overhead, `cap − margin` is not a meaningful
/// threshold, and an always-true trigger would wedge the session into a
/// compact-every-turn state (PR #1695 review). The reactive heal still
/// coalesces toward `max(1, cap − margin)` per refusal — only the
/// pre-emptive gate disarms.
bool messageCapTriggerReached(
  int messageCount,
  int? learnedCap, {
  int margin = kMessageCapDefaultMargin,
}) =>
    learnedCap != null &&
    learnedCap > margin &&
    messageCount >= learnedCap - margin;

